     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I have an app which serves up data from a database in graphical and summary form.  The data are from monitoring sites and the online sites and the parameters measured at each site varies.  I have taken an approach used elsewhere using call and do.call to generate the UI.  My question is, can I use the dynamically created input elements in an observe or reactive construct and have the code respond when any of the elements changes?<br><br>In the example below, stns is populated with the available monitoirng stations and the UI built with a navbarpanel with one panelset for each site.  Within each panelset I have a dateRangeInput and tabset.  Each of the these have a dynamic name.  The crux of the matter is that I would like to update the data set based on changes in the dateRangeInput.  I have not been able to get the observe or reactive construct to recognize changes in the dynamically named dateRangeInputs.  Is this possible?<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">shinyUI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  fluidPage</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    uiOutput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;navUI&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#get the online stations from the db - db left out for example purposes</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>stns</span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">stn1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">NULL<